  "notes": "\"Percussion-forward\" is the entry's own word for the kit and it is what this model is built on: \"a syncopated trap kick, a clap on beat 3 or on 2&4, dense swung 16th hats with triplet rolls, and a prominent live-percussion layer (congas, timbales, shakers, body percussion)\". So `kick.syncopation` is the highest in this batch, the perc lanes are wide and loud, and `fullTimeVariantProb` carries the clap moving to 2&4. \"Stop-time breaks for choreography are a structural device\" is the arrangement's high `dropOutBeats` and `switchUpProb`. The 808 stays and is authored to its stated mix — \"mixed loud and distorted\" — so `distortion` is `medium`, which is the hardest setting in this section. She self-produces, so \"the harmony is keyboard-chosen\": minor 2-chord loops with m9 pads, occasional modal single-chord vamps, and Latin-adjacent `i–VI–VII` figures, all three authored as families. The melody carries \"agile mid-alto with a big gospel belt and heavy rhythmic syncopation; high note-density, runs on every phrase end\" and the sisters' shared trademark of \"very wide self-harmonised stacks used as an instrumental pad\", which is the counter's high `densityRatio`. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**, mirroring the entry's medium-low: \"tempo/drum values are inference\". ⚠ All drum numbers, the swing amount and the 808 figures are **INFERRED**. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
